invariant: INV-26
file: gcm.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: gcm.c guards its GHASH on the carry-less multiply on a macro no
  build defines, so a TCP host object runs the portable 128-step multiply
  on every schedule, which the instructions run. Nothing else objects.
  ghash_hw.c still compiles and links and defines two functions nobody
  calls, and bin/ghash_equiv_test, the published vectors and the
  Wycheproof suite all pass, because the portable GHASH computes the same
  bytes; only the time is wrong, by the factor docs/quic.md measures. The
  design refuses a silent fall back: a host object is a statement about
  what the object contains. The script compiles gcm.c for the TCP suite
  host object and requires its object to call both entries ghash_hw.c
  defines.

--- old
#ifdef GCM_GHASH_CARRYLESS_ALONE
// ghash_hw.c computes both GHASH steps on the carry-less multiply
--- new
#ifdef CH_GHASH_HW
// ghash_hw.c computes both GHASH steps on the carry-less multiply
